            <h3>Weekday vs Weekend Schedule</h3>

            <p>Weekdays: The Piedmont operates its full schedule with four daily round-trip departures, providing excellent flexibility for commuters and business travelers. The Carolinian adds a daily option. Weekday travel tends to attract professionals commuting between Charlotte and the Piedmont Triad.</p>
            <p>Weekends: The Piedmont maintains its full weekend schedule, though the atmosphere is more relaxed with leisure travelers, families, and tourists. The Carolinian also operates on weekends. Overall, weekends provide the same frequency with a more sightseeing-oriented atmosphere.</p>
            <p>Overall, weekdays offer slightly more business-focused travel, while weekends provide a relaxed environment for leisure and family trips.</p>
            <h3>Early and Late Train Availability</h3>

            <p>First Trains: The earliest Piedmont train (Train 71) departs Charlotte around 6:30 AM, arriving in Greensboro by approximately 8:00 AM. The Carolinian departs Charlotte around 6:45 AM, arriving in Greensboro around 8:24 AM - perfect for early meetings or maximizing your day.</p>
            <p>Last Trains: The last Piedmont train (Train 77) departs Charlotte around 3:27 PM, arriving in Greensboro around 4:50 PM. The last northbound Piedmont (Train 76) departs Charlotte around 7:45 PM, arriving in Greensboro around 9:05 PM. This provides flexibility for evening events or late business dinners.</p>
            <p>Direct Service: All trains on this route run direct with no transfers required, making travel simple.</p>
